WEBVTT

00:00:00.262 --> 00:00:02.603
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Saj and Rebecca are both doctors

00:00:02.603 --> 00:00:07.931
and they’ve been together for nine years. She’s a vegan, he’s not.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:11.389
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> When I see anyone eat meat, but in particular Saj,

00:00:11.389 --> 00:00:14.398
it’s a thing that’s quite hard to describe to people who aren’t vegan.

00:00:14.541 --> 00:00:17.958
It’s not just nauseating and kind of a little bit gross,

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.667
it’s also something, kind of, profoundly hurtful,

00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:24.202
so it’s even worse watching someone that you love doing that

00:00:24.202 --> 00:00:26.823
and I think that’s where the tolerance has to come from.

00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:30.930
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> My favourite meaty meal is a chicken teriyaki.

00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:34.135
Like, that’s the thing that I really hanker for.

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:40.027
So, if I’m finishing work, I walk past this Japanese restaurant

00:00:40.193 --> 00:00:43.191
and they’ve got just this most amazing chicken teriyaki.

00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:45.343
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Do you tell Rebecca about it when you get home?

00:00:45.724 --> 00:00:51.396
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> Um, no I – I usually don’t. Just depends on how brave I’m feeling.

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:55.433
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> I went to meet Saj and Rebecca at their flat in south-east London.

00:00:55.925 --> 00:00:59.843
Occasionally, Saj smuggles in some milk chocolate desserts,

00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:03.940
but, other than that, this is a meat- and dairy-free zone.

00:01:04.178 --> 00:01:06.852
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> Tonight is, well, it’s Friday, so it’s fish and chip night.

00:01:06.954 --> 00:01:10.121
So, we’re having a vegan version with some vegan scampi.

00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:13.334
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> And can I see this fake scampi that you’re going to cook?

00:01:14.261 --> 00:01:17.567
So, rehydrated textured soy and wheat protein.

00:01:18.382 --> 00:01:21.079
Saj, when you look at this, does your heart fill with joy?

00:01:21.104 --> 00:01:22.761
Would you prefer real scampi bites?

00:01:22.761 --> 00:01:26.228
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> Yeah, I really like scampi, but my heart doesn’t go,

00:01:26.227 --> 00:01:27.545
‘Oh God, give me the real stuff!’

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.799
I’ll just be like, right, let’s try it, bring it on.

00:01:30.551 --> 00:01:32.584
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Come on, would you not prefer some sausages?

00:01:33.115 --> 00:01:37.125
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> Um, ooh, yeah, if they’re going.

00:01:37.245 --> 00:01:39.711
But if I’m eating with Beck I always think that…

00:01:40.401 --> 00:01:42.871
it’s, like, one of my rules that we should eat together

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.851
and we should always have the same meal.

00:01:44.994 --> 00:01:48.035
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> At first, Rebecca would eat a little bit of fish

00:01:48.035 --> 00:01:50.331
and chicken when she was with Saj,

00:01:50.593 --> 00:01:53.490
even occasionally cooking him sausages.

00:01:53.755 --> 00:01:56.484
But she never felt entirely comfortable with it

00:01:56.484 --> 00:01:59.062
and eventually stopped eating meat altogether.

00:01:59.943 --> 00:02:02.693
Then, two and a half years ago, she became vegan,

00:02:02.876 --> 00:02:07.175
motivated by her strong feelings about animal welfare and the environment.

00:02:07.802 --> 00:02:13.373
She says over time it’s become increasingly hard to watch Saj eat meat.

00:02:13.515 --> 00:02:14.770
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> I know that he eats meat,

00:02:14.795 --> 00:02:19.260
but because he doesn’t do it very often in front of me I don’t have to deal with it,

00:02:19.285 --> 00:02:21.627
so I can kind of just pretend it’s not happening.

00:02:22.135 --> 00:02:24.519
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Some people listening might be thinking,

00:02:24.638 --> 00:02:27.426
‘How can you actually be in a relationship with someone

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:31.883
when you find a part of their life morally repugnant?’

00:02:33.354 --> 00:02:36.832
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> I think because we’ve been together so long,

00:02:36.832 --> 00:02:39.312
and Saj is the most important person in my life

00:02:39.313 --> 00:02:44.531
and he’s made huge efforts to not eat a lot of meat and dairy and he is, kind of,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.488
shifting more towards my way of thinking, it makes it a little bit more tolerable.

00:02:48.805 --> 00:02:51.398
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> When did you last see Saj eat meat?

00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:53.470
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> The weekend before last.

00:02:54.018 --> 00:02:55.219
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> And where were you?

00:02:55.219 --> 00:02:57.179
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> Er, we went to visit my parents.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.525
And it’s like the worst situation that he could have done it in as well,

00:02:59.525 --> 00:03:01.701
’cause I’ve been telling my mum, who’s also vegan,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.839
‘Oh, Saj is great, he’s eating hardly any meat these days.’

00:03:03.839 --> 00:03:06.500
And then we went out for Chinese and he ordered pork dumplings

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.382
and I just didn’t make eye contact with my mum.

00:03:08.644 --> 00:03:14.793
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> And, Rebecca, when you watched Saj eat the pork, how did that feel?

00:03:18.237 --> 00:03:20.059
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> I guess it’s a mix of annoyance,

00:03:20.059 --> 00:03:23.398
’cause I really wish he didn’t eat it, and sadness,

00:03:23.423 --> 00:03:28.197
’cause I thought that you weren’t eating pork much any more and I, like, love pigs.

00:03:28.442 --> 00:03:32.820
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Now, apparently, they didn’t row about it on the way home.

00:03:33.035 --> 00:03:38.087
For these two, it’s love before lamb chops, tenderness before teriyaki.

00:03:38.611 --> 00:03:42.792
But, if Rebecca had been a vegan when they first met,

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:46.104
would this relationship have ever got off the ground?

00:03:46.374 --> 00:03:48.409
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> I think my militance would get on your nerves

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:50.998
and your meat eating would be intolerable for me.